text:
@GregAbbott_TX 
@realDonaldTrump 

Can you both look into weather events and cloud seeding? It seems to me the public has no information about whether this is governed by the states or the federal government. We need a nationwide understanding of the pros and cons, where it’s done, who’s getting paid for this, what are taxpayers funding, how is it regulated, who maintains the data on its short and long-term effects:

Texas has seven state-run cloud seeding programs covering 31 million acres, regulated by the Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation (TDLR). These programs target convective clouds to enhance rainfall, typically from April to September, but operations are suspended during flash flood warnings or excessive rainfall to avoid exacerbating floods.

